    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "Eligibility criteria were structured using the PICo framework (population, interest and context), which is appropriate for non-clinical and policy-focused research questions: Population (P) : national health systems, institutions and stakeholders involved in OH implementation. Interest (I) : challenges, opportunities, barriers, facilitators and implementation strategies related to OH integration. Context (Co) : human, animal and environmental health sectors at national or sub-national levels. This review includes peer-reviewed studies published between 1 June 2013, and 1 April 2025... Only peer-reviewed journal articles published in English were included.",
      "reason": "The text specifies the PICo framework components, settings (national/sub-national, human/animal/environmental), publication dates, language, and publication status, which covers the required study characteristics for eligibility."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "This review includes peer-reviewed studies published between 1 June 2013, and 1 April 2025... Only peer-reviewed journal articles published in English were included. Conference abstracts lacking full-text availability were excluded due to insufficient methodological detail... Grey literature was also excluded to ensure methodological consistency and comparability across included studies.",
      "reason": "The text explicitly specifies dissemination year (2013-2025), language (English), and publication/report status (peer-reviewed, full-text, exclusion of grey literature)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The text describes reasons for exclusion (inaccessibility, disease-specific focus, conceptual discussions) but does not explicitly distinguish between exclusion because outcomes were not measured versus exclusion because outcome results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_11",
      "quote": "Data were synthesized narratively in alignment with the structure of the results section, beginning with study characteristics followed by thematic analysis of challenges, opportunities and recommendations. Challenges, opportunities and recommendations were identified through iterative coding of extracted data.",
      "reason": "The text specifies the groups used in the synthesis (challenges, opportunities, recommendations) which align with the review objectives to synthesize evidence on these topics."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_34",
      "quote": "Institutional reports, governmental policy documents and technical briefs were excluded to maintain methodological rigour and comparability across studies. Although this strengthens internal validity and reproducibility, it may have limited inclusion of operational insights from national OH platforms that are not disseminated through peer-reviewed channels.",
      "reason": "The text provides a clear rationale for the notable restriction of excluding grey literature (methodological rigour and comparability)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
